  {
   "text": "The Marvel Super Heroes Welcome Decks are five monocolored thirty-card ready-to-play sample decks . The decks were designed for Two-Headed Giant and became available as part of the Avengers Academy events in the US and Canada from June 12-18, 2026.",
   "scene": 0,
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "The Welcome decks consist of basic lands , commons , 4 uncommons and 1 mythic rare . They are provided for free to newcomers in a pack that contains two of these decks and instructions.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "These 30-card decks can be provided by an LGS to new players during Open House events or for walk-in demos. There are two decks in each box; one in an indicated color, and the other a random one of the five mana colors in Magic . After the demo experience, the new player can take home their deck free-of-charge to continue their Magic journey. Designed as a tool for new player acquisition, the decks also include a peek at some Booster Fun cards (with 2 Booster Fun cards in each deck), plus a way to play against a friend or mentor until they get the hang of the rules.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Similar to Jumpstart packs , a player can pick any two Welcome Decks, shuffle them together, and instantly have a 60-card deck to play with. Players are encouraged to use the mix-and-match gameplay as a mechanically simple way to demonstrate color combinations and variety in deck strategy.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "The five decks each feature a different iconic Marvel character as a mythic rare card that's new to Magic . These are available only in these Welcome Decks and in Marvel Super Heroes Collector Boosters .",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "The expansion code used by Wizards of the Coast for these decks is WD6.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
